Have a seat.

268
00:16:40,188 --> 00:16:41,188
Shoot.

269
00:16:43,313 --> 00:16:44,730
Sorry for dropping by.

270
00:16:46,230 --> 00:16:49,188
I couldn't get in touch with you,
and I got worried.

271
00:16:49,938 --> 00:16:51,521
I took the plunge and came by.

272
00:16:53,230 --> 00:16:54,230
Well…

273
00:16:54,896 --> 00:16:57,105
Things have just been busy.

274
00:16:57,188 --> 00:16:58,188
Ow, that's hot!

275
00:16:59,813 --> 00:17:02,146
Can I take your word for that?

276
00:17:03,521 --> 00:17:04,521
Huh?

277
00:17:05,188 --> 00:17:06,188
It's just…

278
00:17:07,563 --> 00:17:09,396
I thought you hated me.

279
00:17:10,563 --> 00:17:13,688
That's not it.

280
00:17:13,771 --> 00:17:14,605
Not at all.

281
00:17:17,355 --> 00:17:18,646
That's good then.

282
00:17:22,896 --> 00:17:24,605
-Are you interested?
-Huh?!

283
00:17:26,521 --> 00:17:27,938
In <i>Kenseikitan</i>.

284
00:17:31,521 --> 00:17:34,605
One of my clients likes it,
so I've been studying up on it.

285
00:17:35,105 --> 00:17:36,521
-Here you go.
-Thanks.

286
00:17:37,105 --> 00:17:38,688
I see.

287
00:17:39,188 --> 00:17:41,396
It's really popular, isn't it?

288
00:17:42,063 --> 00:17:44,063
Is Hijiri-kun their <i>oshi</i>?

289
00:17:46,188 --> 00:17:47,105
You know about it?

290
00:17:48,771 --> 00:17:50,230
We're covering it right now.

291
00:17:50,313 --> 00:17:51,480
I see.

292
00:17:54,563 --> 00:17:55,771
Like this.

293
00:17:57,105 --> 00:18:02,730
Hijiri-kun's fans bought out
a digital billboard for his birthday.

294
00:18:04,521 --> 00:18:06,355
That's amazing.

295
00:18:06,938 --> 00:18:09,146
I think they're lucky

296
00:18:10,521 --> 00:18:14,355
to be able to devote themselves
like that to someone.

297
00:18:17,480 --> 00:18:19,355
Even if it's a 2D character,

298
00:18:20,521 --> 00:18:24,146
I wish I could love someone
that sincerely.

299
00:18:37,230 --> 00:18:39,063
Have you

300
00:18:40,230 --> 00:18:42,646
never had someone like that?

301
00:18:45,730 --> 00:18:47,938
I wouldn't say never.

302
00:18:51,146 --> 00:18:54,605
But I don't think I've ever had
a real romance.

303
00:18:57,730 --> 00:19:01,771
A lot of people approach me
because I'm on TV a lot.

304
00:19:01,855 --> 00:19:03,938
And I learn the hard way.

305
00:19:05,688 --> 00:19:07,646
Sometimes I get serious,

306
00:19:08,146 --> 00:19:11,855
but once we sleep together, they ghost me.

307
00:19:16,855 --> 00:19:19,521
So I became scared of love.

308
00:19:34,271 --> 00:19:35,730
You take trains, huh?

309
00:19:35,813 --> 00:19:36,688
What?

310
00:19:37,188 --> 00:19:38,813
You're a public figure though.

311
00:19:39,771 --> 00:19:43,188
Of course I take trains.
I'm still just a company employee.

312
00:19:45,146 --> 00:19:46,563
But just in case…

313
00:19:48,438 --> 00:19:49,563
There.

314
00:19:52,688 --> 00:19:56,855
What do your patients
come to your clinic for?

315
00:19:57,355 --> 00:19:58,646
Things like ED?

316
00:20:02,063 --> 00:20:04,313
We do get a lot
of erectile dysfunction cases.

317
00:20:05,230 --> 00:20:07,105
If you include mild cases,

318
00:20:07,188 --> 00:20:09,521
they say 18 million men in Japan have it.

319
00:20:09,605 --> 00:20:11,021
That many?!

320
00:20:15,313 --> 00:20:17,188
Do you have female patients too?

321
00:20:18,271 --> 00:20:20,063
Yeah. Not that many though.

322
00:20:22,646 --> 00:20:23,521
I'm glad.

323
00:20:24,521 --> 00:20:25,355
Huh?

324
00:20:27,021 --> 00:20:28,980
They have someone they can talk to.

325
00:20:30,438 --> 00:20:32,730
Women have sexual concerns too.

326
00:20:33,396 --> 00:20:34,688
And sexual desires.

327
00:20:42,771 --> 00:20:44,855
If you ever want to talk, I'm here.

328
00:20:47,355 --> 00:20:49,021
Do you mean it?

329
00:20:49,105 --> 00:20:51,771
You haven't even read any of my messages.

330
00:20:51,855 --> 00:20:54,896
I mean it.
I'll reply properly from now on.

331
00:20:56,355 --> 00:20:57,605
I'm kidding.

332
00:21:11,355 --> 00:21:13,771
Women have sexual desires too.

333
00:22:09,230 --> 00:22:10,188
<i>Don't run away.</i>

334
00:22:10,271 --> 00:22:12,938
You should get
deeply involved with someone.

335
00:22:13,521 --> 00:22:15,855
Someone who isn't your patient.

336
00:22:23,355 --> 00:22:26,688
YUMI ICHINOSE

337
00:22:26,771 --> 00:22:30,521
UNBLOCK?
CANCEL / UNBLOCK

338
00:22:33,396 --> 00:22:34,896
UNBLOCK

339
00:22:35,396 --> 00:22:37,396
YOU HAVE UNBLOCKED YUMI ICHINOSE

340
00:22:59,730 --> 00:23:01,855
Hey, Yuta?

341
00:23:01,938 --> 00:23:04,480
Are you ever gonna work
at your family's hospital?

342
00:23:06,021 --> 00:23:07,063
Why would I?

343
00:23:07,563 --> 00:23:09,021
There's no way.

344
00:23:09,105 --> 00:23:12,480
I've cut ties with my parents
and my brother.

345
00:23:12,563 --> 00:23:15,021
Your brother's running it now, right?

346
00:23:16,980 --> 00:23:19,980
Even if I asked to work there,

347
00:23:20,771 --> 00:23:22,396
he wouldn't want me there.

348
00:23:23,313 --> 00:23:25,230
Not that I'd ever ask.

349
00:23:25,730 --> 00:23:27,230
I see.

350
00:23:27,730 --> 00:23:29,313
That's a relief.

351
00:23:29,396 --> 00:23:30,396
Yeah?

352
00:23:31,771 --> 00:23:33,730
I like living in Tokyo.

353
00:23:38,646 --> 00:23:40,146
Anyway,

354
00:23:40,230 --> 00:23:42,521
I'm glad you got transferred
to dermatology.

355
00:23:43,563 --> 00:23:48,730
Back when you were in psychiatry,
you looked completely overwhelmed.

356
00:23:51,105 --> 00:23:52,438
Plus,

357
00:23:53,021 --> 00:23:56,313
it didn't seem like
you had time for this stuff.

358
00:23:59,771 --> 00:24:00,771
Yeah.

359
00:24:03,980 --> 00:24:07,980
I can't tell her I'm working
for a doctor who's basically a weirdo,

360
00:24:08,063 --> 00:24:11,438
doing work that's turning me
into a weirdo too.

361
00:24:11,521 --> 00:24:14,355
We have a customer
who's a fan of yours, Koropokkuru!

362
00:24:14,438 --> 00:24:15,855
Really?!

363
00:24:15,938 --> 00:24:17,146
Now, little lost one.

364
00:24:17,230 --> 00:24:19,605
I'll cast a spell to make it extra tasty.

365
00:24:19,688 --> 00:24:25,063
Here! <i>Runerune firifiri moyamoya rin</i>!

366
00:24:25,146 --> 00:24:27,521
Here's your magic powder!

367
00:24:31,646 --> 00:24:32,563
Hey, old man.

368
00:24:32,646 --> 00:24:34,146
I'm Koropokkuru.

369
00:24:35,480 --> 00:24:36,980
Why are you working here?

370
00:24:38,938 --> 00:24:40,146
W-Why?

371
00:24:41,813 --> 00:24:43,438
Stay away from Mio.

372
00:24:43,521 --> 00:24:44,688
What?

373
00:24:45,646 --> 00:24:48,396
I said stay away from Mio!

374
00:24:48,480 --> 00:24:50,813
Huh? Mio?

375
00:24:50,896 --> 00:24:52,146
You're an Undine fan?

376
00:24:52,230 --> 00:24:54,855
Then come when she's working.
She'll be here later--

377
00:24:54,938 --> 00:24:57,688
I don't care! Just quit already, old man!

378
00:24:58,646 --> 00:25:00,230
O-Old man?

379
00:25:07,646 --> 00:25:10,730
Fairies don't have ages either.

380
00:25:11,938 --> 00:25:12,980
Manager…

381
00:25:19,896 --> 00:25:24,688
A guy friend came on to you,
and that's what got you into this?

382
00:25:27,021 --> 00:25:30,563
We're in the same grade,
and we're both into anime.

383
00:25:30,646 --> 00:25:32,480
We even went to events together.

384
00:25:33,480 --> 00:25:36,521
Then one day,
he said he wanted to come over.

385
00:25:37,980 --> 00:25:40,980
I wanted to show him
my collection and stuff, so…

386
00:25:43,313 --> 00:25:44,813
And then…

387
00:25:46,146 --> 00:25:47,271
All of a sudden,

388
00:25:48,021 --> 00:25:49,480
he kissed me

389
00:25:50,146 --> 00:25:51,688
and started touching my chest.

390
00:25:52,355 --> 00:25:54,313
I got scared and told him no,
and he said,

391
00:25:54,396 --> 00:25:56,271
"Then why did you let me in?"

392
00:25:59,021 --> 00:26:03,313
If I'd had sex with him back then,

393
00:26:03,396 --> 00:26:07,021
maybe we'd still be friends now.

394
00:26:07,521 --> 00:26:09,855
I kept thinking that over and over.

395
00:26:13,938 --> 00:26:17,105
And that was when you really got into

396
00:26:17,188 --> 00:26:18,396
Hijiri-kun?

397
00:26:19,105 --> 00:26:22,355
2D characters will never
look at me that way.

398
00:26:22,438 --> 00:26:25,105
Even without touching each other,

399
00:26:26,438 --> 00:26:28,230
we can still feel connected.

400
00:26:29,688 --> 00:26:33,313
That said, I <i>do </i>look at Hijiri that way.

401
00:26:35,396 --> 00:26:38,605
But deep down, I understand.

402
00:26:40,230 --> 00:26:41,480
After all,

403
00:26:41,980 --> 00:26:43,980
my periods started late.

404
00:26:44,813 --> 00:26:46,146
I'm still just a kid.

405
00:26:46,980 --> 00:26:51,188
I have to step into the real world
someday to grow up.

406
00:26:51,938 --> 00:26:53,605
No. That's not--

407
00:26:55,230 --> 00:26:56,646
Crap! My shift!

408
00:26:56,730 --> 00:26:59,146
All right. These are for you.

409
00:26:59,230 --> 00:27:00,063
Are you sure?

410
00:27:00,146 --> 00:27:02,646
Yeah. Take care of them, okay?

411
00:27:02,730 --> 00:27:04,938
Oh, Micchi's coming by today.

412
00:27:05,021 --> 00:27:06,146
Micchi?

413
00:27:06,230 --> 00:27:08,355
He's become my fan lately.

414
00:27:08,438 --> 00:27:10,230
I used to be all about <i>oshikatsu</i>,

415
00:27:10,313 --> 00:27:12,938
but being someone's <i>oshi</i>
is actually pretty fun too.

416
00:27:13,438 --> 00:27:15,105
I talk too much in here.

417
00:27:15,188 --> 00:27:16,730
I'd better go!

418
00:27:16,813 --> 00:27:18,396
Thank you.

419
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:20,188
Take care of them, okay?

420
00:27:21,146 --> 00:27:23,438
Yay, I gave them to him!

421
00:27:31,105 --> 00:27:32,355
This is for you.

422
00:27:34,855 --> 00:27:35,688
Next time…

423
00:27:43,646 --> 00:27:45,271
<i>You're meeting outside the café?</i>

424
00:27:45,355 --> 00:27:48,771
Yeah. But we're just going
to a Kenseikitan event.

425
00:27:48,855 --> 00:27:51,396
-Really?
-I thought you didn't do outside dates.

426
00:27:51,480 --> 00:27:52,438
I did too.

427
00:27:52,938 --> 00:27:55,271
I figured Micchi might be okay.

428
00:27:55,355 --> 00:27:57,771
Well, he's a really big fan of yours.

429
00:27:57,855 --> 00:28:00,105
But just stick to the event, okay?

430
00:28:00,188 --> 00:28:01,563
No karaoke or anything.

431
00:28:01,646 --> 00:28:03,146
Private rooms are a no-go.

432
00:28:03,230 --> 00:28:05,230
Yeah. I know.

433
00:28:05,313 --> 00:28:07,438
By the way, Micchi's cute, right?

434
00:28:07,521 --> 00:28:08,938
-You think so too?
-Yeah.

435
00:28:09,021 --> 00:28:10,563
Is he older than us?

436
00:28:10,646 --> 00:28:13,521
He said he's a fourth-year in college.

437
00:28:13,605 --> 00:28:15,146
-Oh.
-He's smart!

438
00:28:27,896 --> 00:28:29,771
I'm heading out.

439
00:28:30,938 --> 00:28:31,771
Natsume.

440
00:28:35,063 --> 00:28:37,813
You mentioned that you
sometimes make clothes, right?

441
00:28:39,105 --> 00:28:39,938
Yes.

442
00:28:40,980 --> 00:28:43,813
Do you think you could make
something like this?

443
00:29:03,438 --> 00:29:04,521
Undine.

444
00:29:05,980 --> 00:29:07,855
Or should I say, Mio?

445
00:29:07,938 --> 00:29:08,813
Did you wait?

446
00:29:10,105 --> 00:29:11,438
All right. Let's go.

447
00:29:11,521 --> 00:29:13,271
The end of the line's that way.

448
00:29:15,480 --> 00:29:16,688
Not there.

449
00:29:18,938 --> 00:29:22,146
I came here by car,
so let's go for a ride.

450
00:29:28,521 --> 00:29:29,730
But…

451
00:29:31,938 --> 00:29:34,146
I don't wanna get into a car.

452
00:29:34,230 --> 00:29:38,271
Really? But the line's huge.

453
00:29:39,813 --> 00:29:41,271
And it's hot here.

454
00:30:17,105 --> 00:30:17,938
Shukuchi.

455
00:30:33,896 --> 00:30:36,105
Sorry to keep you waiting, Mio.

456
00:30:37,271 --> 00:30:38,980
Doctor…

457
00:30:39,646 --> 00:30:41,605
Who the hell are you?

458
00:30:42,771 --> 00:30:45,855
She's a minor.
Where do you think you're taking her?

459
00:30:52,855 --> 00:30:55,063
If it's to protect her,

460
00:30:56,896 --> 00:30:58,938
I'll cut down anyone, even a god!

461
00:30:59,521 --> 00:31:01,730
Wow!

462
00:31:01,813 --> 00:31:04,105
What the hell? You creep!

463
00:31:07,438 --> 00:31:09,480
Doctor, how did you…?

464
00:31:09,563 --> 00:31:11,480
Well, Saikawa--

465
00:31:12,188 --> 00:31:14,771
I mean, Koropokkuru told me.

466
00:31:18,605 --> 00:31:21,813
I was so scared.

467
00:31:24,688 --> 00:31:25,813
It's okay.

468
00:31:25,896 --> 00:31:28,313
I got carried away with
being someone's <i>oshi</i>--

469
00:31:31,730 --> 00:31:34,438
Don't come near Mio
dressed like that, you creep!

470
00:31:34,521 --> 00:31:35,563
-It's pathetic!
-Takeru!

471
00:31:35,646 --> 00:31:37,313
Stop, Takeru!

472
00:31:37,396 --> 00:31:40,021
He's a doctor from the clinic!
He helped me!

473
00:31:42,355 --> 00:31:45,605
Could you be…

474
00:31:47,355 --> 00:31:48,521
Ow…

475
00:32:01,896 --> 00:32:03,063
Thank you.

476
00:32:03,146 --> 00:32:04,146
No problem.

477
00:32:06,521 --> 00:32:09,355
You were keeping an eye
on the Fairy Café, right?

478
00:32:15,063 --> 00:32:16,521
That place

479
00:32:17,021 --> 00:32:21,188
had shady rumors about girls
sugar dating outside the café.

480
00:32:23,605 --> 00:32:25,438
Just like Hijiri-kun would,

481
00:32:25,938 --> 00:32:29,355
