from danger, weren't you?

482
00:32:32,980 --> 00:32:34,605
I wasn't…

483
00:32:36,188 --> 00:32:39,271
Instead of protecting her,
I ended up hurting her.

484
00:32:42,146 --> 00:32:45,105
I like 2D characters too,

485
00:32:46,105 --> 00:32:48,646
but it's not like
I'm not interested in real people.

486
00:32:50,188 --> 00:32:52,563
I thought Mio felt the same way.

487
00:32:55,480 --> 00:32:58,230
I figured it was okay
since she let me into her room.

488
00:33:00,271 --> 00:33:03,605
You ended up lashing out
because you were embarrassed.

489
00:33:07,271 --> 00:33:10,480
But after that,
I looked into a lot of things.

490
00:33:11,146 --> 00:33:13,563
I learned what "sexual consent" is.

491
00:33:18,771 --> 00:33:21,230
You learned that being alone
in a room with someone

492
00:33:21,313 --> 00:33:25,355
doesn't mean they're consenting to sex.

493
00:33:27,563 --> 00:33:28,396
Yes.

494
00:33:33,396 --> 00:33:36,188
Mio…

495
00:33:38,855 --> 00:33:40,771
I'm really sorry.

496
00:33:44,396 --> 00:33:47,605
I hope we can go back to being friends.

497
00:34:01,396 --> 00:34:05,021
You don't have to
give your answer right now.

498
00:34:20,188 --> 00:34:22,063
I know it's kind of late to ask,

499
00:34:22,563 --> 00:34:24,855
but why are you cosplaying as Hijiri-kun?

500
00:34:29,813 --> 00:34:32,021
Listening to you talk about him,

501
00:34:32,105 --> 00:34:33,771
I became a fan too.

502
00:34:35,355 --> 00:34:37,271
Dressing up like Hijiri-kun

503
00:34:37,355 --> 00:34:39,896
gave me a little more courage than usual.

504
00:34:57,771 --> 00:34:58,771
Then…

505
00:35:01,521 --> 00:35:04,938
Starting today,
the three of us are <i>oshikatsu </i>buddies.

506
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:08,105
Huh?

507
00:35:12,438 --> 00:35:15,021
Why don't we go inside,
since we're already here?

508
00:35:17,605 --> 00:35:19,938
Drink it up. You too, Doctor.

509
00:35:20,021 --> 00:35:20,938
Okay.

510
00:35:22,730 --> 00:35:24,855
Come on. Do you want liquid sugar?

511
00:35:25,896 --> 00:35:27,188
I'm okay.

512
00:35:39,063 --> 00:35:41,396
I found my first real-life <i>oshi</i>.

513
00:35:44,355 --> 00:35:45,355
What?

514
00:35:46,688 --> 00:35:49,188
Thank you, Doctor.

515
00:35:49,271 --> 00:35:52,605
-Doctor, scoot a little closer.
-Oh, okay.

516
00:35:54,688 --> 00:35:57,021
I should be thanking you.

517
00:35:59,021 --> 00:36:03,146
Love can take many different forms.

518
00:36:04,313 --> 00:36:05,980
I think you taught me that.

519
00:36:08,355 --> 00:36:09,313
Ready?

520
00:36:09,396 --> 00:36:11,230
-Yes.
-Yes.

521
00:36:12,063 --> 00:36:17,521
Even without a physical relationship,
people can still connect emotionally.

522
00:36:19,396 --> 00:36:22,813
You gave me a prescription, Mio.

523
00:36:28,313 --> 00:36:29,605
A prescription?

524
00:36:30,313 --> 00:36:32,230
You had it rough,

525
00:36:32,730 --> 00:36:34,271
Koropokkuru.

526
00:36:34,355 --> 00:36:36,396
Seriously, stop calling me that.

527
00:36:37,521 --> 00:36:40,396
It's crazy how invested
the doctor gets in all this.

528
00:36:40,480 --> 00:36:42,563
Yeah. It's a problem, huh?

529
00:36:42,646 --> 00:36:43,896
It's frustrating.

530
00:36:43,980 --> 00:36:45,271
Okay, that's enough.

531
00:36:45,355 --> 00:36:47,521
No. I'm taking about myself.

532
00:36:48,188 --> 00:36:50,188
I'm frustrated with myself.

533
00:36:51,313 --> 00:36:55,021
He drags me around,
but I end up seeing his point.

534
00:36:56,105 --> 00:36:58,521
And I'd get a little emotional too.

535
00:37:00,438 --> 00:37:02,730
You two might actually make a good match.

536
00:37:03,230 --> 00:37:06,396
I see why Professor Kurusu
recommended this place for you.

537
00:37:08,021 --> 00:37:09,271
Please stop.

538
00:37:09,355 --> 00:37:12,646
I'm gonna find something else to do
and quit being a nurse.

539
00:37:12,730 --> 00:37:14,230
Oh, yeah?

540
00:37:14,313 --> 00:37:17,313
Saikawa, Natsume,
you can head out now.

541
00:37:17,396 --> 00:37:18,813
Thank you for today.

542
00:37:21,271 --> 00:37:22,188
<i>Because I love my </i>oshi<i>.</i>

543
00:37:23,230 --> 00:37:27,646
<i>If you don't tell someone</i>
<i>you love them, they won't know.</i>

544
00:37:27,730 --> 00:37:29,563
<i>Don't you think so?</i>

545
00:37:30,771 --> 00:37:32,480
Oh, a feature on Hijiri-kun?

546
00:37:32,563 --> 00:37:33,438
<i>You're right.</i>

547
00:37:33,521 --> 00:37:35,938
You're really into it now, huh?

548
00:37:36,521 --> 00:37:38,396
Oh, yes.

549
00:37:38,480 --> 00:37:41,230
-Who was this reporter again?
-Huh?

550
00:37:41,313 --> 00:37:42,480
Ichinose?

551
00:37:42,563 --> 00:37:43,855
Oh, that's right.

552
00:37:43,938 --> 00:37:45,438
She's pretty, isn't she?

553
00:37:46,438 --> 00:37:47,896
Totally my type.

554
00:37:47,980 --> 00:37:50,563
Saikawa, Natsume,
you can head out now.

555
00:37:50,646 --> 00:37:51,813
Wait a minute.

556
00:37:51,896 --> 00:37:54,688
Wasn't the lady who called the doctor
also named Ichinose?

557
00:37:54,771 --> 00:37:56,938
-What?
-Oh, you're right.

558
00:38:03,188 --> 00:38:04,605
Good work today.

559
00:38:09,230 --> 00:38:11,813
Huh? Wait. No way.

560
00:38:12,438 --> 00:38:13,438
There's no way.

561
00:38:13,521 --> 00:38:15,855
No, absolutely not.

562
00:38:21,188 --> 00:38:23,813
So, how is he doing?

563
00:38:25,605 --> 00:38:29,188
I can't say due to
patient confidentiality.

564
00:38:31,813 --> 00:38:35,688
Patient? Isn't he more like
an experiment to you?

565
00:38:35,771 --> 00:38:39,688
Don't say that.
You make it sound scandalous.

566
00:38:41,230 --> 00:38:42,230
Well…

567
00:38:46,896 --> 00:38:49,355
I'll be watching to see
how this plays out.

568
00:39:09,896 --> 00:39:10,980
Shimotori?

569
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:14,855
Yes. This is Shimotori.

570
00:39:16,980 --> 00:39:18,771
You called me.

571
00:39:21,271 --> 00:39:22,605
Um…

572
00:39:23,646 --> 00:39:25,271
If you're okay with it,

573
00:39:26,813 --> 00:39:29,438
I was hoping we could meet again.

574
00:39:31,230 --> 00:39:35,480
<i>Even without a physical relationship,</i>
<i>people can still connect emotionally.</i>

575
00:39:37,355 --> 00:39:41,146
<i>I wonder if the prescription I gave</i>
<i>might work on me too.</i>

576
00:39:42,771 --> 00:39:44,355
I'm impressed.

577
00:39:45,146 --> 00:39:48,146
People actually talk about
things like sexual consent.

578
00:39:49,938 --> 00:39:51,438
With all that in mind,

579
00:39:51,521 --> 00:39:56,230
some people might think
love isn't worth the effort.

580
00:39:57,688 --> 00:40:01,771
But I think there's
that much value in love.

581
00:40:46,730 --> 00:40:48,563
-Sorry.
-Sorry.

582
00:40:50,521 --> 00:40:51,688
We got soaked.

583
00:40:53,563 --> 00:40:56,105
I shouldn't have insisted on
going to another bar.

584
00:40:57,021 --> 00:40:57,938
It's okay.

585
00:40:58,480 --> 00:41:01,480
This guerrilla rainstorm
came out of nowhere.

586
00:41:02,646 --> 00:41:03,646
Localized heavy rain.

587
00:41:04,896 --> 00:41:05,896
What?

588
00:41:07,396 --> 00:41:09,146
Localized heavy rain.

589
00:41:09,646 --> 00:41:12,480
"Guerrilla" isn't really a nice term.

590
00:41:14,480 --> 00:41:17,396
Just what I'd expect
from a former weather presenter.

591
00:41:18,563 --> 00:41:19,771
Stop it.

592
00:41:22,938 --> 00:41:23,855
Here.

593
00:41:26,563 --> 00:41:27,563
Thanks.

594
00:41:31,063 --> 00:41:32,480
What should we do?

595
00:41:33,188 --> 00:41:34,813
We might catch a cold.

596
00:41:35,938 --> 00:41:37,230
That's true.

597
00:41:38,938 --> 00:41:40,188
I'll go get a taxi.

598
00:41:54,855 --> 00:41:56,480
If you don't tell them,

599
00:41:58,021 --> 00:41:59,438
they won't know.

600
00:42:01,896 --> 00:42:03,355
Shimotori!

601
00:42:24,896 --> 00:42:25,896
Sorry.

602
00:42:28,355 --> 00:42:29,771
Even for a kiss,

603
00:42:30,605 --> 00:42:32,771
you need sexual consent, right?

604
00:42:41,771 --> 00:42:42,771
I…

605
00:42:45,188 --> 00:42:46,938
I like you.

606
00:42:49,271 --> 00:42:50,438
I liked you back then,

607
00:42:51,980 --> 00:42:52,980
and I still do.

608
00:42:58,605 --> 00:42:59,813
So…

609
00:43:07,188 --> 00:43:08,188
So…

610
00:45:15,563 --> 00:45:17,480
Subtitle translation by: Yuki Asami

